---
// How one imagined push flows through the system, drawn by hand: the real frame goes through
// V-JEPA 2 once; pushes chain in latent space; the translator turns each latent into text.
// Shapes from src/jat/wm/encoder.py and models.py. The default slot is the caption.
---

<figure class="pipeline wide">
  <div class="scroll">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 380" role="img" aria-labelledby="pipe-title pipe-desc">
    <title id="pipe-title">The world model behind the simulate tool</title>
    <desc id="pipe-desc">
      A table image goes through V-JEPA 2, frozen, into a latent of 64 tokens by 1,024 numbers. The
      predictor takes a latent and a push and gives the next latent, again and again. The
      translator reads each latent and writes the state as text for the LLM, which sends back the
      next plans.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="pipe-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="ink-fill" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- the real frame -->
    <g transform="translate(20,40)">
      <rect width="120" height="120" rx="8" class="table-fill" />
      <path d="M38,44 h44 v11 h-16.5 v33 h-11 v-33 h-16.5 z" class="t-fill" transform="rotate(-18 60 60)" />
      <text x="60" y="142" class="label">real frame</text>
      <text x="60" y="160" class="sub">256 × 256 px</text>
    </g>
    <path d="M150,100 h46" class="flow" marker-end="url(#pipe-arrow)" />

    <!-- V-JEPA 2 -->
    <g transform="translate(205,50)">
      <rect width="130" height="100" rx="10" class="box meta" />
      <text x="65" y="44" class="name">V-JEPA 2</text>
      <text x="65" y="66" class="sub">ViT-L, frozen</text>
      <text x="65" y="84" class="sub">Meta</text>
    </g>
    <path d="M345,100 h46" class="flow" marker-end="url(#pipe-arrow)" />

    <!-- the latent: an 8 x 8 token grid -->
    <g transform="translate(400,40)">
      {
        Array.from({ length: 64 }, (_, i) => (
          <rect x={(i % 8) * 15} y={Math.floor(i / 8) * 15} width="12" height="12" rx="2" class="token" />
        ))
      }
      <text x="58" y="142" class="label">latent z₀</text>
      <text x="58" y="160" class="sub">64 tokens × 1,024</text>
    </g>

    <!-- predictor chain -->
    <path d="M530,100 h40" class="flow" marker-end="url(#pipe-arrow)" />
    <g transform="translate(578,50)">
      <rect width="130" height="100" rx="10" class="box trained" />
      <text x="65" y="40" class="name">Predictor</text>
      <text x="65" y="62" class="sub">z + push → next z</text>
      <text x="65" y="80" class="sub">6-layer transformer</text>
    </g>
    <path d="M610,6 v36" class="flow push" marker-end="url(#pipe-arrow)" />
    <text x="600" y="22" class="sub end">push (start → end)</text>
    <path d="M718,100 h40" class="flow" marker-end="url(#pipe-arrow)" />
    <g transform="translate(766,62)">
      {
        Array.from({ length: 16 }, (_, i) => (
          <rect x={(i % 4) * 19} y={Math.floor(i / 4) * 19} width="15" height="15" rx="2" class="token imagined" />
        ))
      }
      <text x="36" y="98" class="label">ẑ₁, ẑ₂, …</text>
    </g>
    <path d="M880,100 h20 q20,0 20,-20 v-40 q0,-20 -20,-20 h-210 q-10,0 -10,10 v12" class="flow loop" marker-end="url(#pipe-arrow)" />
    <text x="940" y="64" class="sub left">chain</text>
    <text x="940" y="80" class="sub left">pushes</text>

    <!-- translator and the LLM -->
    <path d="M800,150 v50" class="flow" marker-end="url(#pipe-arrow)" />
    <g transform="translate(720,210)">
      <rect width="160" height="80" rx="10" class="box trained" />
      <text x="80" y="34" class="name">Translator</text>
      <text x="80" y="56" class="sub">latent → state</text>
    </g>
    <path d="M710,250 h-90" class="flow" marker-end="url(#pipe-arrow)" />
    <g transform="translate(320,212)">
      <rect width="300" height="76" rx="10" class="box text-box" />
      <text x="16" y="30" class="mono">I2 = R0 + push (190, 248) → (190, 348)</text>
      <text x="16" y="52" class="mono">T center (250, 376), angle 327°</text>
    </g>
    <path d="M320,250 h-90" class="flow" marker-end="url(#pipe-arrow)" />
    <g transform="translate(60,210)">
      <rect width="160" height="80" rx="10" class="box meta" />
      <text x="80" y="34" class="name">Muse Spark</text>
      <text x="80" y="56" class="sub">the agent (LLM)</text>
    </g>
    <path d="M140,300 v40 h503 v-190" class="flow plans" marker-end="url(#pipe-arrow)" />
    <text x="390" y="358" class="sub">simulate(from_frame, plans): the next pushes to imagine</text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="numbered">
    <slot>
      <span class="key meta"></span> Meta model &nbsp; <span class="key trained"></span> trained during
      the hackathon. The image goes through V-JEPA 2 once. Imagined pushes stay in latent space: no
      image is ever generated. The LLM only reads the translator's text.
    </slot>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  /* on a phone the diagram keeps a readable size and scrolls sideways */
  .scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .pipeline svg {
    min-width: 720px;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
  }
  .box {
    fill: var(--surface);
    stroke: var(--axis);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  .box.meta {
    stroke: var(--meta);
    stroke-width: 2.5;
  }
  .box.trained {
    stroke: var(--trained);
    stroke-width: 2.5;
  }
  .text-box {
    stroke-dasharray: 4 3;
  }
  .table-fill {
    fill: var(--table);
    stroke: var(--axis);
  }
  .t-fill {
    fill: var(--t-real);
  }
  .token {
    fill: var(--meta);
    opacity: 0.55;
  }
  .token.imagined {
    fill: var(--ghost);
    opacity: 0.35;
    stroke: var(--ghost);
  }
  .flow {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--muted);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }
  .flow.loop,
  .flow.plans {
    stroke-dasharray: 5 4;
  }
  .flow.push {
    stroke: var(--pusher);
  }
  .ink-fill {
    fill: var(--muted);
  }
  text {
    text-anchor: middle;
    fill: var(--text);
  }
  .name {
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  .label {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .sub {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    fill: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .left {
    text-anchor: start;
  }
  .end {
    text-anchor: end;
  }
  .mono {
    text-anchor: start;
    font: 12px ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace;
    fill: var(--text-secondary);
  }
</style>
